--TEST--
an enum case spelled as a lowercase keyword is still a case, so its one error is its casing — `rule:core-api/casing-checks-the-leading-character`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Mode {
    Plain,
    default,
    list,
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0110]: `default` must be PascalCase, e.g. `Default`
  --> case.nvs:4:5
%A
error[E0110]: `list` must be PascalCase, e.g. `List`
  --> case.nvs:5:5
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
